title: S2D/HCI production monitoring
agents: windows
catalog: storage/hci
license: PolyForm Internal Use 1.0.0
distribution: check_mk

description:
 Production-hardened read-only monitoring for Windows Failover Clustering,
 Storage Spaces Direct, HCI storage, and optional Hyper-V workloads. Collector
 protocol version 1 provides explicit run IDs and collector-health records.
 Cluster-wide data is emitted by one deterministically elected node to a stable
 logical cluster piggyback host. Optional VM data is emitted to stable VM-GUID
 piggyback hosts so live migration does not churn service identity.

item:
 Storage and cluster services use stable collector identities. Human-readable
 object names are retained in service summaries. Parser errors, duplicate
 identities, protocol mismatches, and structured command failures become visible
 UNKNOWN services instead of silently disappearing.

inventory:
 Services are discovered from the s2d_hci_* data sections and from
 <<<s2d_hci_collector_health>>>. Hyper-V workload sections are disabled by
 default and must be explicitly enabled through the Agent Bakery configuration
 or the bounded JSON configuration.

perfdata:
 Metrics are provided for CSV/volume free percentage, storage-pool allocated
 bytes, storage-job progress, VM CPU usage, VM memory pressure, and checkpoint
 age. The removed performance-history collector is intentionally not packaged.

parameters:
 Rules configure CSV and volume free-space thresholds, VM CPU/memory and
 checkpoint-age thresholds, and the operational-state severity policy used for
 degraded, paused, draining, offline, and unknown Microsoft states.

troubleshooting:
 First inspect the S2D/HCI collector-health services on physical cluster nodes.
 A failed, incomplete, or truncated collector run is explicitly visible there.
 Inspect raw agent output for protocol_version=1 and a consistent run_id. Cluster
 data appears on the logical s2d-cluster-* piggyback host. Custom VM data appears
 on s2d-vm-<guid> piggyback hosts only when virtualization collection is enabled.
 Verify required FailoverClusters, Storage, ActiveDirectory, and Hyper-V modules
 for the selected deployment mode.
